endobj
241 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (The overall analysis highlights Meta Facebook as the primary driver of incremental revenue, accounting for over 44% of total channel contribution. However, this media channel also exhibits one of the lowest marginal ROIs, suggesting that it is almost saturated. Instead, Google Paid Search, Google Shopping, and Google PMax deliver a ROI greater than 1 and represent the most efficient platforms for future investments. Moreover, the saturation analysis shows that Google Video, Meta Facebook, and Meta Instagram produce diminishing returns, meaning that increasing the budget in these areas will not lead to much more growth.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
242 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (To maximize future revenue and optimize budget allocation for the next quarter, instead of simply increasing total spend, the most effective strategy prioritises advertising investment in those channels that have not yet reached their saturation point. Indeed, the investment simulation across four different scenarios reveals that an allocation strategy that manages the budget in under-performing and saturated platforms, by redistributing it across the top performing channels, yields the highest return on investment.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
243 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 139 0 R
/E (Ultimately, the best approach toward revenue maximization is to focus on the efficiency of marketing investments rather than on the overall volume. In particular, staying active on social platforms is essential for brand awareness and perception, but further spending should address direct search channels where customers play an active role.   )
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
244 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (Causal Assumptions)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
