>>
endobj
247 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (First, credible intervals are used to quantify the range of plausible values for ROI and mROI estimates, as Meridian adopts a Bayesian probabilistic approach. Then, the definition of a surrogate model to better interpret the MMM through SHAP analysis may introduce slight discrepancies due to the different modelling approaches underlying the two models. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (Data Quality)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
249 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/E (The advertising spend and revenue data are already aggregated at a daily level, requiring no additional transformation. Moreover, some missing values are included for media channel variables, such as spend, clicks, and impressions. However, they are simply imputed with a value of zero, assuming that they represent a total absence of advertising activity rather than a data collection error.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
