792 0 obj
<<
/Title (Media Spend Trend The organisation allocates its marketing budget across 9 different channels, which vary in both coverage and total investment. In particular, Facebook is the main media channel, accounting for approximately $ 4.9 million, over 54% of the total spend, with active campaigns throughout the entire period. Then, Google Paid Search is the second largest channel, representing about 17% of the total investment with $ 1.5 million.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 790 0 R
/Next 794 0 R
>>
endobj
793 0 obj
<<
/Title (In particular, Google channels, including Paid Search, Shopping, and PMax, show high probabilities, ranging from 92% to 97%, of delivering a positive return. Looking at their response curves, these channels are currently performing well despite being under-invested. Instead, Meta Facebook and Google Video show lower probabilities, below 50%, of achieving a ROI greater than 1. Based on their current spend levels and the diminishing returns shown in their response curves, the company may be over-investing in these areas.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
