797 0 obj
<<
/Title (Correlation Analysis The correlation matrix shows how different variables interact each other. As expected, there is a strong positive correlation between spending, clicks, and impressions associated with each media channel, suggesting that marketing budget allocation attract users across all platforms. Moreover, the plot displays also a positive correlation between overall marketing spend and purchase metrics, related to revenue and order volumes, highlighting the impact of media investment toward sales. In contrast, non-paid media channels appear isolated from other marketing activities. Indeed, while these channels are strongly correlated with one another, they do not show any meaningful connection to daily changes in advertising spend.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 794 0 R
/First 799 0 R
/Last 799 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 800 0 R
>>
endobj
798 0 obj
<<
/Title (ROI and mROI Tables Considering both ROI and marginal ROI for each marketing channel, along with their corresponding credible intervals, Google Paid Search emerges as the most efficient platform, with an ROI of 1.80 and an mROI of 0.90, followed by other media like Google Shopping and Google PMax. In contrast, Meta Facebook is the main driver of revenue volumes, but it shows less efficiency with an ROI of 1.05 and an mROI of 0.43. Therefore, while Meta is essential for reaching large volumes, Google provides the best return for future investments.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 801 0 R
/Next 795 0 R
>>
