802 0 obj
<<
/Title (Model Configuration After the preprocessing step, the Meridian framework requires to map each variable to its role, distinguishing between paid media, organic media, and non-media treatments, together with the integration of the holdout index. Regarding the model specification, LogNormal priors were defined for each channel ROI, as they ensures positive estimates and models the typical right-skewness of marketing performance. In this context, specific location and scale parameters were applied by assigning higher expectations to search and shopping channels, while adopting broader distributions for video and social platforms. Moreover, the knot scaling was enabled to ensure the model is able to automatically capture the temporal variations in media effectiveness. Ultimately, the model was trained using a Bayesian MCMC approach by performing both prior sampling to validate the model assumptions and posterior sampling to extract reliable parameter estimates.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 800 0 R
/Next 804 0 R
>>
endobj
